My mistake! The old code does return an AST, which is also the behaviour in Parcel@1:
```
      `module.exports=${JSON.stringify(	
        gql([...gqlMap.values()].join('\n')),	
        null,	
        2,	
      )};`
```
This was not obvious to me in the above code. Using `gql` vs `parse` and the `join`.

I can make a separate issue to further discuss this as it is a breaking change. I feel like `v1` -> `v2` is the perfect time to make this breaking change.

---

I feel like a string is a much more usable return type:
-   It is ready to send to the server, so that the user does not need to have the `graphql` package on the frontend to format the value before use. Is the AST is desired it can be parsed.
